[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Sticky Fingers]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.52]What two interruptions did the writer have? | 作者遇到了哪两次打扰？
[00:15.83]After breakfast, I sent the children to school and then I went to the shops. | 早饭后，我送孩子们上学，然后就去了商店。
[00:23.02]It was still early when I returned home. | 我回到家时，时间还早。
[00:27.30]The children were at school, my husband was at work and the house was quiet. | 孩子们在上学，我丈夫在上班，家里静悄悄的。
[00:34.05]So I decided to make some meat pies. | 于是我决定做些肉馅饼。
[00:38.34]In a short time I was busy mixing butter | 不一会儿我就忙着调和黄油
[00:41.82]and flour and my hands were soon covered with sticky pastry. | 和面粉了，很快手上就沾满了黏黏的面糊。
[00:47.98]At exactly that moment, the telephone rang. | 正在这个时候，电话铃响了。
[00:53.28]Nothing could have been more annoying. | 没有什么比这更恼人的了。
[00:56.75]I picked up the receiver between two sticky fingers and was dismayed when I recognized the voice of Helen Bates. | 我用两根黏糊糊的手指夹起了听筒，听出是海伦·贝茨的声音，真让我沮丧。
[01:08.01]It took me ten minutes to persuade her to ring back later. At last I hung up the receiver. | 我花了10分钟才说服她过会儿再打来。我终于挂上了电话。
[01:17.22]What a mess! There was pastry on my fingers, on the telephone, and on the doorknobs. | 真是糟糕透了！我的手指上、电话机上、门的把手上都沾上了面糊。
[01:27.01]I had no sooner got back to the kitchen than the doorbell rang loud enough to wake the dead. | 我刚回到厨房，门铃又响了起来，响得足以把死人吵醒。
[01:35.88]This time it was the postman and he wanted me to sign for a registered letter! | 这回是邮递员，他要我签收一封挂号信！
